FYDE: drm/v3d: plumb a per-client scheduler priority (currently disabled)

What this patch originally did -- the global 'latest_job' chain that made
every client's bin job wait on the last job submitted by any other client --
has been removed; see 052 for why it appeared to help and what the real
problem was.

What remains is the groundwork for giving each DRM client its own
drm_sched_entity priority instead of DRM_SCHED_PRIORITY_NORMAL for
everyone, so that the compositor can outrank background app rendering.
The uid-based selection is left #if 0'd: keying off the ARC uid range is
too fragile to enable, and the intended interface is for userspace to ask
for a priority explicitly.

Index: v6.12-rpi/drivers/gpu/drm/v3d/v3d_drv.c
